# SY1SY2: the DSP join of the ARM pitch word and the 16-bit table entry into the Stage B step.
#
# ISR step 3 (0x1C0679..0x1C06E6) computes  step = ratio(e) * 0.05 / word  with
#   e    = low 16 bits of DM(0x9354A + index)   (index = low half of pair word 0, 0x36 -> 0x93580)
#   word = DM(0x921A6), the pair-block pitch word the ARM sends (boot value 0x3D4CCCCD = 0.05)
# docs/research/synth-sample-kernel-rule.md section 13. Edit the two pokes for another point.
# Run:  sharc-ref sy.bin tools/oracle_scenarios/sy_pitch_join.scn --out target/oracle/join
#       the `step` series is the record word 0x9242D (step / 2^24 = ratio); expected for
#       e = 0x0800 (ratio 0.625), word = 0x3C748500 (key 60, tune -946): 0x21809F8.
meta rate 48000
warmup 0x1c0b2d 100000 flag12=1
irq 13
msg 0x92414 0x1c07cd
irq 17
fill 0xC0000 128 sine stride=2 freq=0.0625 amp=0.5
fill 0xC0001 128 sine stride=2 freq=0.0625 amp=0.5
poke 0x93580 0x0800
poke 0x921a6 0x3c748500
irq 13
msg 0x92414 0x1c084c
loop 12
poke 0x92410 0x200
irq 17
capture step 0x9242d 1
capture word 0x921a6 1
capture entry 0x93580 1
end
